{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 21,
  "title": "Hanuma consoles Tara",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga21/kishkindhasans21.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga21/kishkindhaitrans21.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Hanuma tries to console Tara. He asserts that Angada will not be looked down. Though Vali is put to his plight, Hanuma says, that Tara alone is the empress to lead Kishkindha kingdom. But Tara prefers self-immolation along with her husband Vali."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे एक विंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 21st chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.21.1",
      "label": "4.21.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "ततो निपतिताम् ताराम् च्युताम् ताराम् इव अंबरात् |\nशनैः आश्वासयामास हनूमान् हरि यूथपः",
      "iast": "tato nipatitām tārām cyutām tārām iva ambarāt |\nśanaiḥ āśvāsayāmāsa hanūmān hari yūthapaḥ",
      "translation": "Hanuma, the leader of monkeys, then neared and slowly consoled Tara who has fallen to ground like a star from sky.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "tataH",
          "iast": "tataḥ",
          "devanagari": "ततः",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ambaraat cyutaam taaraam iva",
          "iast": "ambarāt cyutām tārām iva",
          "devanagari": "अम्बरात् च्युतां तारां इव",
          "meaning": "from sky, fallen, a star, like",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "nipatitaam taaraam",
          "iast": "nipatitām tārām",
          "devanagari": "निपतितां तारां",
          "meaning": "fallen to ground, at Tara",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "hari yuuthapaH hanuumaan",
          "iast": "hari yūthapaḥ hanūmān",
          "devanagari": "हरि यूथपः हनूमान्",
          "meaning": "monkey's, leader, Hanuma",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 9
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shanaiH aashvaasayaamaasa",
          "iast": "śanaiḥ āśvāsayāmāsa",
          "devanagari": "शनैः आश्वासयामास",
          "meaning": "slowly, consoled.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.21.2",
      "label": "4.21.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "गुण दोष कृतम् जंतुः स्वकर्म फल हेतुकम् |\nअव्यग्रः तद् अवाप्नोति सर्वम् प्रेत्य शुभ अशुभम्",
      "iast": "guṇa doṣa kṛtam jaṃtuḥ svakarma phala hetukam |\navyagraḥ tad avāpnoti sarvam pretya śubha aśubham",
      "translation": "\"Living beings on doing the deeds of merit or demerit, or knowingly or unknowingly, will derive the resultant fruits of those deeds according to one's own destiny even after demise, and they shall bear them unrepentantly, may they be provident or improvident...",
      "notes": [
        "For this verse Dharmaakuutam says: <em>atra ca sva karama phala hetukamiti viśeṣaṇena anādi bhava parampara āsādita dharma artha vāsanā vaśena śubham aśubham vā karma anuṣṭhāya tad aurūpam sukaham duḥkham vā phalam avāpnoti iti uktam -- dharmākūtam</em>Thus Hanuma is saying that Vali is not dead at the hand of Sugreeva but dead due his own demerits."
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "jantuH",
          "iast": "jantuḥ",
          "devanagari": "जन्तुः",
          "meaning": "living beings",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "guNa doSa kR^itam",
          "iast": "guṇa doṣa kṛtam",
          "devanagari": "गुण दोष कृतं",
          "meaning": "merit, demerit, doings [whether done in good intention or bad]",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "phala hetukam",
          "iast": "phala hetukam",
