          "iast": "a vyagraḥ avāpnoti",
          "devanagari": "अ व्यग्रः अवाप्नोति",
          "meaning": "un, repentantly, one gets.",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.21.3",
      "label": "4.21.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "शोच्या शोचसि कम् शोच्यम् दीनम् दीना अनुकंपसे |\nकः च कस्य अनुशोच्यो अस्ति देहे अस्मिन् बुद्बुद उपमे",
      "iast": "śocyā śocasi kam śocyam dīnam dīnā anukampase |\nkaḥ ca kasya anuśocyo asti dehe asmin budbuda upame",
      "translation": "\"Of which lamentable one you lament while you yourself are in a lamentable state? Of which pitiable one you take pity while you yourself are in a pitiable condition? Who is pitiable by whom in these bubbles like bodies?",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "shocyaa",
          "iast": "śocyā",
          "devanagari": "शोच्या",
          "meaning": "a lamentable [you yourself]",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shocyam kam shocasi",
          "iast": "śocyam kam śocasi",
          "devanagari": "शोच्यं कं शोचसि",
          "meaning": "lamentable one, about whom, you are lamenting",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
