    {
      "id": "4.21.10",
      "label": "4.21.10",
      "numbers": [
        10
      ],
      "devanagari": "संततिः च यथा दृष्टा कृत्यम् यत् च अपि सांप्रतम् |\nराज्ञः तत् क्रियताम् सर्वम् एष कालस्य निश्चयः",
      "iast": "santatiḥ ca yathā dṛṣṭā kṛtyam yat ca api sāmpratam |\nrājñaḥ tat kriyatām sarvam eṣa kālasya niścayaḥ",
      "translation": "\"Whatever duty anticipated from a male descendent towards his father, and whatever activity that is to be done presently in respect of the dying king, let them be done, and that would be a timely decision.",
      "notes": [
        "This expression also means <em>smaśāna vyrāgya</em> 'burial-ground renunciation...' In that, 'all this has happened so according to Time's decision...' <em>arthā gṛhāt nivartante ā smaśānāt tu bāndhava | sukṛtam duṣkṛtam caiva gaccantam anucacchgati ||</em>'wealth and means remain in house, relatives come up to graveyard, only Merit and Demerit follow the goer...'"
      ],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "santatiH yathaa dR^iSTaa",
          "iast": "santatiḥ yathā dṛṣṭā",
          "devanagari": "सन्ततिः यथा दृष्टा",
          "meaning": "progeny, as to how, seen kin scriptures - anticipated from a male descendent",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
